# Cloudflare Pages routing.
#
# The app routes in memory (`createMemoryHistory`), so it has no deep links of its own and would
# seem not to need a fallback at all. It needs exactly one, and losing it breaks sign-in rather
# than navigation: Aegis returns from OAuth to `/callback?code=…`, which is a real request to this
# origin for a path no file exists at. Without this line Pages answers it with a 404 and the code
# is spent on an error page — the user is bounced back to sign-in with nothing said.
#
# `webAuth.cleanUpUrl()` puts the address bar back to `/` immediately afterwards, which is why this
# is the only path that ever needs rewriting and why it is worth writing down: nothing else in the
# app will remind anyone that it does.
#
# 200, not 302: the browser must keep the URL it asked for, because the query string carries the
# authorization code the page is about to read.
#
# Static files are matched before this — Pages serves what exists first — so `overlay.html`,
# `screencast-overlay.html` and everything under `assets/` are unaffected.
/*    /index.html   200
